<title>CHINA: Tientsin Marine 96 net up 39.45 pct.</title>
<headline>Tientsin Marine 96 net up 39.45 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of yuan unless stated, against 1995 figures)</p>
<p> Turnover	   490.656	  vs	  320.786</p>
<p> Net profit	  97.472	  vs	  69.897</p>
<p> Net asset per share     2.28  yuan   vs   1.79  yuan</p>
<p> Earnings per share	0.418 yuan   vs   0.488 yuan</p>
<p>(The company listed its B shares on April 30, 1996)</p>
<p>Company name: Tientsin Marine Shipping Co Ltd.</p>
<p>Note: the results were published in a company statement on Thursday. All figures are based on domestic accounting standards. Figures based on international accounting standards were not available.</p>
<p>The company's board of directors proposed no cash dividend or bonus shares, pending approval of a shareholders meeting.</p>
</text>
